    "text": "(Well-known problem). Suppose that F is an automorphism of order 2 of the\npolynomial ring Rn = C[x1 , . . . , xn ], n > 2. Does there exist an automorphism G\nof Rn such that G−1 F G is a linear automorphism?\n   This is true for n = 2.                                          M. V. Neshchadim",
